IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa08-types`

-- Pensions Act 2008 (UK) — GOAL 3: PENALTY NOTICES (ss 40-41).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2008-30.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — penalty notices`

-- s 40(4) "The penalty— (a) is to be determined in accordance with
-- regulations, and (b) must not exceed £50,000." (5)(b): the payment date
-- "must be at least 4 weeks after the date on which the notice is issued".
@ref s 40(4)-(5)
`the maximum fixed penalty` MEANS 50000

@ref s 40(5)(b)
@export The earliest date a fixed penalty notice under s 40 of the Pensions Act 2008 (UK) may set for payment: 4 weeks (28 days) after the date the notice is issued. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc The date the fixed penalty notice was issued
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest payment date for` f MEANS
    Date (Day (f's `fixed penalty notice issued on`) PLUS 28)

@ref s 40(4)(b)
GIVEN f IS A `Penalty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fixed penalty is within the limit in` f IF
    f's `fixed penalty amount` AT MOST `the maximum fixed penalty`

-- s 41(2) "the Regulator may not issue an escalating penalty notice if— (a)
-- ... the person ... has applied for a review ... and any review has not been
-- completed; (b) ... the person has exercised the right of referral to a
-- tribunal ... in respect of a fixed penalty notice ..., and the reference has
-- not been determined."
@ref s 41(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Penalty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an escalating penalty notice may be issued under` f IF
        NOT (f's `a review of the underlying notice is pending`)
    AND NOT (f's `a tribunal reference about the fixed penalty is pending`)

-- s 41(5) the daily rate "must not exceed £10,000"; (6)(d) the start date
-- "must not be earlier than the date specified in the fixed penalty notice";
-- (6)(e) payable at the daily rate "until the date on which the person
-- complies". Days from the start date up to (not including) compliance.
@ref s 41(4)-(6)
@export The escalating penalty payable under s 41 of the Pensions Act 2008 (UK): the daily rate (at most £10,000) for each day from the date it is payable until the date of compliance (excluding that date); 0 if a notice may not be issued, the daily rate exceeds £10,000, or the start date is earlier than the fixed penalty notice's payment date allows. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc The fixed penalty issue date, pending reviews or references, the start date, the daily rate and the compliance date
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the escalating penalty under` f MEANS
    IF       `an escalating penalty notice may be issued under` f
         AND f's `daily rate` AT MOST 10000
         AND f's `escalating penalty payable from` AT LEAST `the earliest payment date for` f
         AND days GREATER THAN 0
    THEN days TIMES f's `daily rate`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        days MEANS Day (f's `complied on`) MINUS Day (f's `escalating penalty payable from`)
